t a good view of  liberia itself  we can see the eldians in the internment  zone are confined by this large wall  which has very blatant parallels to the  elderly and paradise as well  whereas aaron was caged in due to the  dangerous pure titans outside the walls  zeke was caged in by a society that  despises the aldean race  if you think about it this scene in  particular was really ironic  as this cleaner verbally abused the  yeager family and detested the fact that  eldians were still having children  the irony is that out of all the people  in this interaction zeke would grow up  to agree more with the cleaner than his  own parents which is literally the  opposite of why they took him to this  tower  following on from this the anime flashes  forward to when zeke is a warrior  candidate  and at this point in time all the kids  were competing to inherit the beast  titan  the way he struggled to compete reminded  me of a young rhino but it's funny to  compare the reasons they were struggling  reiner arguably had the most desire to  become a warrior out of anyone but he  lacked the natural talent that was  required to be the best  zika on the other hand was blessed with  royal blood and in theory he should have  been the best candidate out there  but he lacked the drive to actually  become a warrior a young commander  mcgath noted that it was almost like he  didn't want to be there  and the former beast titan seemed to  agree as well this beast titan was tom  sava  and i've already spoken about his full  backstory in a different video that you  might want to check out  from observing zeke on a couple of  occasions tom felt immense sympathy for  the boy  as he could tell from the beginning that  being a warrior is not something he  wanted to do  as a researcher tom thought the concept  of becoming a titan shifter for war was  pointless  and the only reason he got his shifter  was so that he could learn things from  the memories of previous beast titans  he and zeke were therefore similar in  that they lacked the desire to fight for  mali  and by playing catch together they built  a father-son relationship over the years  zeke was lacking a proper father figure  at home because grisham simply used his  son as a tool  to fulfill the plan of the elding  restorationists we saw how zeke's  parents would constantly leave him at  his grandparents house  while they attended their restorationist  meetings and rather than playing with  his son  grisha used all the boy's free time to  study instead one of the worst parts  about this  was that zeke would be studying in  school learning marley's version of  history  then he would be sent to his  grandparents pretty much every night  where he would then learn the same  version of history again  only to then go back home and learn a  different version of that same history  from the perspective of the earlier  restorationists you can imagine that as  a child who doesn't really want to be a  warrior anyway  all of that conflicting information  would be incredibly stressful which is  why you was so excited to maybe read  something else instead  back at training commander mcgath had  been monitoring zeke's lack of progress  for a while  and effectively expelled him due to a  lack of desire  in the commander's words marley would  never give a title to a candidate like  him  but by pure coincidence this was the  same day that zeke first encountered tom  there was a nice bit of foreshadowing  here as salva tells the boy that he'd  make a good pitcher  and in the future zeke's pitching  assault became his main weapon as the  beast titan  i doubt either of them thought this  would be the end result of them playing  catch  but life comes at you fast an important  thing to note is that zeke playing with  someone was such a rarity  that he ran home excitedly to tell his  parents that just gives you some idea of  how his childhood was anything but  normal  and it actually led to one of my  favorite moment