that aaron's father  is a missing doctor called jaeger  he deduced that his father had survived  being sent to the island and the eren  must have been indoctrinated in the same  way that he was  that's why in season 3 he said they were  both victims of grisha because he  assumed his brother was forced to become  an elden restorationist  although as we know that is just not  true another detail is how reina  mentioned that aaron's father left info  in shiganshina  and there's a reason i love this part  specifically obviously reiner and berto  have no idea who aaron's father is as  far as they know he was just a regular  guy who was born on the island  to zeke though he knows from personal  experience that grisham would have left  something relevant to the alien  restorationist  and because he thinks that aaron has  been brainwashed that's why he was so  confident that aaron would return to the  basement soon  next thing to explain about this episode  is aaron apparently betraying the people  of parodies island  because up until now we thought he was  fighting to save them from the outside  world  but now it seems like he's doing the  opposite by helping zeke to end the  aldian race  the question is why would aaron agree to  do something like this when it seems  fundamentally opposed to his nature  and there are two possible answers which  we'll get to in a minute when talking to  his brother  aaron refers to this incident when he  kisses stories hand as back then he  unlocked the full memory of when grisha  killed the royal family his facial  expression indicated he had seen  something super messed up and here he  talks about how he felt the royal  children being squashed like bugs  this is where the conversation takes an  unexpected turn because aaron fully  acknowledges that grisha had to squash  their children  otherwise aaron himself would have been  eaten by the royal family by now  in this moment aaron admits that  grisha's actions allowed him to live  and unlike the royal family he is not  restricted by the vow to announce war  those sound like the words of someone  who agrees with his father's actions yet  in the same breath  erin goes on to say that both he and his  father were wrong his logic is that if  eldings were never born  then they wouldn't have to suffer in the  first place which is the same line of  thinking to both zeke and tom  by saying this he visibly surprises his  brother but also gains his trust  which is necessary if they're going to  make contact as i mentioned there are  only two reasons why aaron would say  what he said  which is that either he does genuinely  believe it or he doesn't and he's just  lying  starting with that first option let's  examine why aaron would actually believe  that it would be better to have never  been born back in the uprising arc  that was the first time that aaron was  told of what his father did and he  showed real remorse for those actions  even going as far as to ask historia to  kill him on top of that  he's also had his fair share of  suffering over the years with of course  the biggest moment  being his mother being eaten by a titan  therefore it is definitely plausible  that aaron could buy into zeke's  ideology  especially as he was already willing to  die for grisha's actions  contrarily he could be lying instead  because zeke's idea to sterilize aliens  is the opposite of freedom  since the beginning aaron has fought for  freedom in many forms first he wanted  the freedom to freely leave the walls  and then once that was accomplished he  wanted parodies to be free of their  enemies from the outside world  if he was to then take away the options  for aliens to reproduce then that is a  forced extermination of their race that  will gradually lead to the end of  society on parodies  this is obviously very different to  eren's usual beliefs so we have to ask  ourselves if he is lying  then what would he gain the answer is  that by gaining his brother's trust  aaron will eventually have access to the  power of the founding titan and as we  know  it is his choice how he wants to use  that power with that said  the episode ends with present day zeke  pulling the trigger on his thunderspear  and blowing both himself and levi  up and also this horse which definitely  did not deserve that we'll see which  characters do or don't survive in the  season finale  but the only thing i really wanted to  say on this was that zeke felt backed  into a corner and would rather risk his  chances of surviving this explosion than  being eaten by a titan like levi  intended  be sure to smash that like button if you  liked the video and i'll see you on  sunday for the last attack on titan  episode review  unless they decide to make a part 2 for  this season by adapting the remaining  manga content  but only time will tell until the next  one peace out
 

